## What is inside

{{types_table}}

| Path | What it is |
| --- | --- |
| `juizdesign.yaml` | The design document: the types of this Component (`juiz pkg design check juizdesign.yaml` checks it) |
| {{design_idl_label}} | The record and enum types (JIDL) the design document uses (`idl:`) |
| `src/{{name}}.zig` | The Component. Each function is a type, listed in `juiz.exportComponent` at the end. Write the bodies (`return error.NotImplemented`) |
| `build.zig` | Builds the plugin `lib{{name}}` with zigjuiz, and puts it with libjuiz_sdk in `zig-out/plugins/` |
| {{design_idl_label}} | `build.zig` generates their Zig types when it builds (`juiz.addTypes`) |
| `build.zig.zon` | The Zig package. It points to zigjuiz (the Zig library of juiz) |
| `app/app.conf` | The configuration to start juiz with. It is also the entry of the `.juizapp` package |
| `app/juizapp.yaml` | The `.juizapp` manifest (name, version, required juiz version) |
| `scripts/dev.sh`, `scripts/dev.ps1` | Build the plugin and put it with libjuiz_sdk in `app/plugins/<target>/` (`--target` / `-Target` for another machine) |
| `scripts/pack.sh`, `scripts/pack.ps1` | Build in release mode and make `dist/{{name}}-<version>.juizapp` |

## Requirements

Linux, macOS or Windows (x86_64). On Windows, use `scripts\dev.ps1` and `scripts\pack.ps1` instead of the `.sh` scripts:
the plugin is `{{name}}.dll`, and `juiz_sdk.dll` goes next to it (Windows has no rpath).
Zig builds it with its default ABI (`x86_64-windows-gnu`); Visual Studio is not needed.

- juiz {{juiz_version}} (`juiz --version`). Install it with `cargo install juiz_app --version {{juiz_version}}` or `pip install juiz-cli=={{juiz_version}}`
- Zig 0.17.x ([ziglang.org](https://ziglang.org/download/), or `pip install ziglang==0.17.1` and `ZIG="python3 -m ziglang" scripts/dev.sh`).
  zigjuiz supports only this version of Zig
- `juiz-idl` or `juiz` in PATH, if `idl:` has {{design_idl_label}}: the build generates the types with `juiz-idl -g zig` (or `juiz idl -g zig`)
- libjuiz_sdk {{juiz_version}} in `{{juiz_sdk_dir}}`. Install it with `juiz sdk install` (`juiz sdk path` prints where it is)
- The juiz source of {{juiz_version}} for zigjuiz, in `{{zigjuiz_dir}}`
- zigjuiz {{juiz_version}}, the Zig library of juiz. `scripts/dev.sh` adds it to `build.zig.zon` the first time (it needs the network once):
  `zig fetch --save=zigjuiz {{zigjuiz_fetch}}`

`build.zig.zon` points to zigjuiz with the path `{{zigjuiz_path}}`, relative to this directory (Zig does not take an absolute path there).
If you move this project or zigjuiz, change the path in `build.zig.zon`.

zigjuiz and libjuiz_sdk must be the same version as juiz: juiz does not load a plugin that carries another version of libjuiz_sdk.
`app/juizapp.yaml` requires `juiz: "={{juiz_version}}"` for the same reason.
When you update juiz, get zigjuiz and libjuiz_sdk of the new version, and change `build.zig.zon` and `app/juizapp.yaml`.
To use libjuiz_sdk in another directory, run `JUIZ_SDK_DIR=<dir> scripts/dev.sh` (`$env:JUIZ_SDK_DIR = "<dir>"` before `scripts\dev.ps1` on Windows, or `zig build -Djuiz-sdk=<dir>`).

## Write, build, run and call

The functions in `src/{{name}}.zig` have the arguments and the return values written in `juizdesign.yaml`, and their bodies are
`return error.NotImplemented`: calling one before you write it fails. The example calls below use the default values, or a value of the type.

```sh
{{next_steps}}
```

A function returns an error (`error.Overflow` and so on) to fail a call; juiz reports it and keeps running.
A panic stops juiz, so the release build keeps the safety checks (ReleaseSafe).

## Changing the design

`juiz pkg create -d` does not change a skeleton it has made. When you change `juizdesign.yaml`, change the functions and the parts of
`juiz.exportComponent` in `src/{{name}}.zig` and `app/app.conf` to match (`juiz pkg create -d juizdesign.yaml -b zig -o <dir>` writes a new skeleton, to copy from).
`juiz pkg add` adds a type to `src/{{name}}.zig` and `app/app.conf`.
`zig build` generates the Zig types of {{design_idl_label}} again when they change (the module `juiz_types`).
When a `.jidl` of `idl:` imports another file, add it to `.depends` of `juiz.addTypes` in `build.zig`.

## Versions

The package version is `0.1.0` in both `build.zig.zon` and `app/juizapp.yaml`. When you release a new version, change both.

## Plugins for several machines in one package

Zig builds for other machines from this one. Install libjuiz_sdk of each target once, build for it, and make the package:

```sh
juiz sdk install --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu
scripts/dev.sh --release --target aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu   # app/plugins/aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu/
juiz sdk install --target aarch64-apple-darwin
scripts/dev.sh --release --target aarch64-apple-darwin        # app/plugins/aarch64-apple-darwin/
scripts/pack.sh                                               # builds for this machine, packs every app/plugins/<target>/
```

The targets are x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, x86_64-apple-darwin, aarch64-apple-darwin and x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.
On Windows, run `scripts\dev.ps1 -Release -Target <target>` and `scripts\pack.ps1`.
Each `app/plugins/<target>/` holds the plugin and libjuiz_sdk of that target.
